  "note": "Election of nine members of the Ballyclare Urban District Council, polled Wednesday 21 May 1958. Fourteen candidates stood; the poll was 61.9 per cent (Belfast News-Letter, 23 May 1958, p. 4). Fourteen candidates for nine seats; poll 61.9 per cent. The local report adds that Mr. Craig topped the poll with 726, Mr. Cameron was second 20 votes behind, Mr. Fleming third with 621, Mr. Herron fifth with 579 and Mr. Douther ninth."
